{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_i3k7suopsqgupzeckjugzmox7jqdf2r4q7ke6vsjlyzxb2you77q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **All checks pass.**\n\n## Bugs found and fixed (4 real divergences)\n\nAll in SSE operand order. The C `.so` is built at `-O0` (no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`), and `mulss`/`addss` propagate the **destination** operand's NaN payload — GCC's choice of destination is *not* the source-text order. I read it out of `objdump -d` rather than guessing:\n\n| function | C codegen | Rust before | fixed to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `c2Mulvs` | `movss xmm0,[a.x]; mulss xmm0,[b]` → dst = lane | `mul_keep_lhs_nan(b, a.x)` | `mul_keep_lhs_nan(a.x, b)` |\n| `c2Dot` y lane | `mulss xmm0,xmm2` → dst = `b.y` | `(a.y, b.y)` | `(b.y, a.y)` |\n| `c2Dot` sum | `addss xmm0,xmm1`, `xmm0` = *y* product | `add(px, py)` | `add(py, px)` |\n| `c2CircletoCircle` + `c2CircletoCapsule` | `addss xmm0,xmm1` → dst = `B.r` | `A.r + B.r` (LLVM commutes freely) | `add_keep_lhs_nan(B.r, A.r)` |\n\nThe pre-existing doc comment claimed `c2Mulvs` was vectorized to `mulps` with the broadcast scalar as destination — it wasn't; that comment was the source of the bug. Corrected in `src/lib.rs` and `ERRORS.md`.\n\n## Gate status\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 12/12 symbols, `comm -23` empty in both profiles; 0 undefined non-libc symbols. Nothing was stubbed; `c_src` is a single 144-line TU, all of it translated.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 55/55 rows pass, ~1.1M randomized comparisons (seeded SplitMix64), compared on **raw bits** so `±0.0` and NaN payloads are distinguished. All 12 entry points driven directly through the `.so`, including the level-0 primitives — which is where every bug was.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 28/28 rows pass, each asserting the *same specific* value, not just \"both failed\". Includes 19 out-of-range enum ints (C's dispatch uses an **unsigned** compare, so negatives also hit `default:`), null pointers, unaligned reads, aliasing, and the unguarded `da / c2Dot(n,n)` division.\n- **Binary** — N/A, no `add_executable`/`[[bin]]` (asserted by `verify.sh`).\n- **Feature combos** — none exist (`verify.sh` derives this from `Cargo.toml`); suite re-run against debug + release, `opt-level` 0/1/2/3/s, `target-cpu=native`, and `lto=fat`: 0 failures, 12 symbols everywhere.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**The suite has proven detection power.** I mutation-tested it — 5 injected bugs (each `c2Dot`/`c2Mulvs` operand order, `f32::max` for the ternary, `typeB==3` accepted, `<=` for `<`) were all caught. Without that check, \"83 tests pass\" wouldn't tell you much.\n\n**Two claims I wrote in Phase A turned out to be wrong, and I corrected them from measurement rather than leaving them in:** I reasoned that the zero-divisor division on capsule branch B was unreachable — it is reachable (10 hits, now asserted `> 0` so the row can't silently stop covering it). And my `err04` aliasing sentinel was wrong, not the Rust: the buffer held a `c2Capsule`, so the blind `*(c2Circle *)A` cast makes `A.r` the capsule's `b.x` at offset 8. That's C behavior to preserve, so I fixed the test.\n\nOne residual gap, documented rather than papered over: `ERRORS.md` row 3's short-buffer case (reading past an unmapped page) is genuine UB and isn't portably observable, so I test the correctly-sized-but-unaligned variant instead."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1101,"cache_read_input_tokens":165495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1101,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46f4400e-8b17-4c31-b920-925dcc4b7b30","uuid":"eeda10b5-f33c-49c9-bd78-4be052df0c18","timestamp":"2026-09-05T07:05:53.823Z"}
